{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/js.rs","issuer":"seat:personal-fold-core-goal","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:41:33.897572Z","id":"52a3439ddce3c4972828782f80acc9f374223b3cf9a221e0635afd1b023bbf3b","body":{"detail":"walk ranks findings by fold id with localeCompare (ICU root collation). The port reproduces ICU's ASCII order (punctuation, digits, letters, case as a tie-break) and orders anything past ASCII by code point after it, where ICU interleaves (é sorts between e and f). Fold ids are slugs today, so goldens cannot see it; an artifact id or page key with non-ASCII would rank differently.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:42b4f3d","suggested_fix":"if ids ever carry non-ASCII, use icu_collator (root, alternate non-ignorable) and add a golden with such ids","summary":"locale_compare matches bun's localeCompare for ASCII only","tags":["parity","session:claude-code:0345f693-a48d-478f-aa49-1df22880dff2"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/walk.rs","issuer":"seat:personal-fold-core-goal","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:41:33.902256Z","id":"366530d7b56f9fc7dc9bed41f895d40b9c3fcea707c7382292e4a22b2147344f","body":{"detail":"For round 3 (home switches the gate's walk onto the core): the caller passes JSON.parse(budgets.json).budgets as opts.budgets and its own zone as opts.localTimeZone, as fold.ts already passes localTimeZone to fold_json. A budgets file without view.words is an error ({error: 'budgets: no view.words'}), where walk.ts would throw on undefined.","kind":"comment","ref":"git:42b4f3d","summary":"walk takes budgets.json's budgets as input; home's walk.ts reads the file itself","tags":["round-3","session:claude-code:0345f693-a48d-478f-aa49-1df22880dff2"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/tz.rs","issuer":"seat:personal-fold-core-goal","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:07:04.206480Z","id":"cf696dc6719924f73b67e10a7d425f71965f6caca543a4a700d03b9cbffbed9f","body":{"detail":"Since 505eea4 the module needs the import js/fold-core.ts core() provides (Intl-backed). home's programs/fold-viewer/core.ts instantiates with {} and would fail to link on its next pin bump: round 3 must switch it to core() or supply the import. Allie's WKWebView has Intl, so the same loader works there.","kind":"comment","ref":"git:505eea4","summary":"the wasm module imports fold_core.tz_offset; a host must answer it","tags":["round-3","session:claude-code:0345f693-a48d-478f-aa49-1df22880dff2"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/sink.rs","issuer":"seat:personal-fold-core-goal","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T01:24:43.473295Z","id":"772fb257ab09ab0dff30f4deb8e237d27969e754a3727b67f037671ca1c2bb2f","body":{"detail":"accept() reads the viewer from the Tailscale-User-Login header, and run() listens on loopback on the assumption that only tailscale serve connects. Nothing checks that: any process on the host (any user, any seat, a browser extension's native host) can open 127.0.0.1:<port> and POST /v or /report with any login it likes, and the sink logs it as that person. The 403 test only covers a missing header, not a forged one. Must be fixed before fold sink is deployed or its log feeds facto (Bobby 20663a55).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:7de2ed5","span":{"start":{"line":67},"end":{"line":67},"content_hash":"b98fd243404f181a17a37671dc82fdacb58c1a7154d5a9034c25f683f0b32c0e"},"suggested_fix":"Take identity from the connection, not a header. Preferred: run the sink as a tsnet node (or behind a listener whose peer is checked) and ask tailscaled LocalAPI whois for the peer address; the login is whois's UserProfile.LoginName, and any Tailscale-User-* header is ignored. Alternative: listen on a Unix socket in a directory only tailscaled's user can open (tailscale serve proxies to unix:), and check SO_PEERCRED/getpeereid is tailscaled's uid. Either way add a forged-header test: a loopback peer that is not the trusted proxy (or whois fails) and sends Tailscale-User-Login: bobby@... gets 403 and logs nothing.","summary":"fold sink trusts Tailscale-User-Login from any loopback peer, so any local process can forge a view or report","tags":["security","before-deploy","session:claude-code:d9087247-b589-43d4-a6ff-3b87fcc717f4"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/html.rs","issuer":"urn:lobby:seat:personal-qualifier-adoption-goal","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T01:20:59.067212Z","id":"1f8447a9fbfa646b9d326e70ea3eba7cb6324c0af1232ce5b4d161068c21ab24","body":{"detail":"Before 2336985 (#18) a row carried about=<haecceity IRI>, so RDFa read every statement on the row element (its class, its link) as a statement about the thing it shows. The row presents the thing; it is not it.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:5ede57a","span":{"start":{"line":106},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"ff7f49a5585f4df8c1a721b79a5827b7745d040490455c615fe7df4949004249"},"suggested_fix":"row resource=#<id> typeof=schema:WebPageElement, with an empty span property=schema:about resource=<IRI>","summary":"about=<IRI> on the row made the row's RDFa statements the data's","tags":["rdfa","semantics","backfill","session:claude-code:a712ec59-2921-4f38-93dd-4df60dcd1593"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/html.rs","issuer":"urn:lobby:seat:personal-qualifier-adoption-goal","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T01:20:59.097579Z","id":"2e4745e2630e118a6eff00b796b52203151b9c1bc9905e6afa4822760f25a971","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2336985","span":{"start":{"line":106},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"ff7f49a5585f4df8c1a721b79a5827b7745d040490455c615fe7df4949004249"},"summary":"fixed in 2336985 (#18): the row is resource=#<id> typeof=schema:WebPageElement with a schema:about span; tests/pages.rs:75 and js/html.test.ts:91 pin the markup; check.yml green at 2336985 (run 41152839271)","supersedes":"1f8447a9fbfa646b9d326e70ea3eba7cb6324c0af1232ce5b4d161068c21ab24","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a712ec59-2921-4f38-93dd-4df60dcd1593"]}}
